From 973cfb163f486ce4a73d4aadfd7726494f5e509d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:37:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NeXT: a window frame after NeXTSTEP, and a theme with it

A new decorator after NeXTSTEP: a one-unit black line round the window;
a title bar, black with a white title while the window is in front and
light grey with a black one behind, the title centred, a miniaturize
button (a small window) at its left and a close button (a cross) at its
right, raised in NeXT's white, grey and black; no zoom button, as there
was none. Under a resizable window, the resize bar: a corner segment at
either end and the middle, raised, parted by black. The buttons work on
a window in the background too.

The borders are not one width, as NeXT's were not: the sides and the top
are the black line (BorderWidth()), the bottom is the resize bar. Stack
and tile and BWindow::DecoratorFrame() count the bottom as the line, so
they see the frame end a little short. With the primary button only the
bar's right segment resizes -- Haiku resizes from the bottom right corner
alone -- and with the secondary all three; the left segment is repainted
when highlighted, which the base class does not do for that corner.

Pixel art in units, like Platinum and Win2k; the title bar is the tab
colour and text, the buttons and the resize bar the border colour, the
bevels white and a half-tone of it.

NeXTSTEP.theme: NeXT's four greys -- black title bars in front, light grey
panels and menus, white where a menu item is chosen, white documents -- on
the dark grey workspace with no picture.

Verified in a guest with StyledEdit, Tracker and a program opening one
window of each look: the bars in front and behind, the buttons and the
resize bar as described; a click on a background window's close button
closed it, miniaturize minimized.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
